<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Qasi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1151</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Qasi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Qasi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> who led the Muridin revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in 1144, seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mertola">Mértola</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> and ruling as an independent lord. He first sought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> help, then turned against them and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> of Portugal. His own followers killed him at Silves in 1151.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi.jpg" alt="Ibn Qasi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguel Vieira [2] · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MertolaCastle2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
